---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SkipLink from '../../components/SkipLink.astro';
import SiteNav from '../../components/SiteNav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What we say publicly — Kala docs"
  description="Our public messaging guidelines. Metrics stay internal until Founder approval."
>
  <SkipLink />
  <SiteNav />
  <main id="main-content" class="doc-page">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="prose">
        <nav class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/docs">Docs</a> / What we say publicly
        </nav>
        <h1>What we say publicly</h1>
        
        <p>
          Kala's public messaging focuses on technical approach and qualitative proof points.
          Quantitative metrics remain internal until approved by the Founder.
        </p>
        
        <h2>Approved messaging</h2>
        
        <h3>Core positioning</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Kala is a CAD agent that ships valid STEP — not a chat that dumps scripts</li>
          <li>Brief in, STEP out</li>
          <li>Reliability you can open in CAD — STEP first</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>Technical approach</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Real tool-calling path through FreeCAD APIs</li>
          <li>Structured commands that produce valid geometry</li>
          <li>Quality gates before delivery: geometry validation, constraint satisfaction, STEP compliance</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>Target use cases</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Mechanical components that need to fit, mate, and manufacture</li>
          <li>Mounts, brackets, flanges, pins, housings</li>
          <li>Hardware engineers, mechanical designers, product teams</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>Honest positioning</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Mid-September 2026 target</li>
          <li>Product still shipping</li>
          <li>No fake benchmarks or competitor comparisons</li>
          <li>No metric headlines until Founder unlocks</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Banned content</h2>
        <p>
          Do <strong>NOT</strong> include in public-facing content:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Quantitative benchmarks or pass rates (e.g., "150/150", "95% success")</li>
          <li>Average scores or performance metrics</li>
          <li>Leaderboards or competitor comparisons</li>
          <li>Pricing tables or cost information</li>
          <li>Fake dashboards or invented data</li>
          <li>Live product demos (until product ships)</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Internal vs. external</h2>
        <p>
          Metrics, benchmarks, and quantitative performance data are tracked internally for development purposes.
          These remain confidential until:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>Product reaches production stability</li>
          <li>Metrics are validated and reproducible</li>
          <li>Founder explicitly approves public disclosure</li>
        </ol>
        
        <h2>Pilot communications</h2>
        <p>
          When communicating with pilot users:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Be honest about development status and limitations</li>
          <li>Share qualitative feedback and learnings</li>
          <li>Request permission before sharing any pilot results publicly</li>
          <li>Keep quantitative results confidential unless approved</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc-page {
    padding: var(--section-padding-desktop) 0;
    min-height: calc(100vh - var(--nav-height) - 20rem);
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    display: block;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }

  .prose {
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .prose h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .prose h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prose ul, .prose ol {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .doc-page {
      padding: var(--section-padding-mobile) 0;
    }
  }
</style>
